target/

# Rust build directories that are **not** the workspace root's.
#
# `target/` above is anchored: dockerignore patterns are matched against the
# path relative to the context root, so it excludes `./target` and nothing else.
# Three of this repository's cargo targets are somewhere else — `edge/` and
# `xtask/spike-impersonate/` are workspaces of their own (RUST_REWRITE_PLAN §3.4)
# and have their own `target/`, and `cargo build` run inside either of them
# creates one there. Unmeasured, that is the difference between a build context of
# about 100 MB and one of 2.4 GB, sent on every build of both `edge/Dockerfile`
# and `crates/freedium-web/Dockerfile`.
#
# It is not only slow. `edge/Dockerfile`'s `build` stage does `COPY . /src` with
# `WORKDIR /src/edge`, so an unexcluded `edge/target` lands exactly where
# `COPY --from=cook /src/edge/target target` is about to put the cooked
# dependencies, and 1.7 GB of stale host artifacts ride along in the layer.
#
# ** is any number of directories including none, so this also covers `target/`,
# which is kept above for a reader who stops at the first matching line.
**/target/

